<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sitabuldi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1817</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-anglo-maratha-war">Third Anglo-Maratha War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sitabuldi was fought on 26–27 November 1817 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagpur">Nagpur</a>, when the forces of the Bhonsle ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mudhoji-ii-bhonsle">Appa Sahib</a> attacked the British Residency and its small garrison on the Sitabuldi hills. The outnumbered Company troops held out, and a further defeat at Nagpur in December broke Appa Sahib's power. Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-anglo-maratha-war">Third Anglo-Maratha War</a>, it led to further losses of territory for the Nagpur kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sitabuldi.jpg" alt="Battle of Sitabuldi" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gppande · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sitabuldi_fort_gate.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
